clapshot-slack-unfurl for Debian
================================

Daemon
------
The package installs a systemd service `clapshot-slack-unfurl.service`,
running as www-data by default. Enable and start it with:

    systemctl enable --now clapshot-slack-unfurl

Configuration
-------------
Config: /etc/clapshot-slack-unfurl.toml (dpkg conffile, chmod 600).
Edit videos_dir and sqlite_path to match your Clapshot data directory.
Upgrades will prompt if the file was locally modified.

Set Slack tokens via environment variables (preferred) by creating
/etc/default/clapshot-slack-unfurl:

    SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=xoxb-...
    SLACK_APP_TOKEN=xapp-...

Then add `EnvironmentFile=/etc/default/clapshot-slack-unfurl` to the
[Service] section of the systemd unit override:

    systemctl edit clapshot-slack-unfurl

Alternatively, uncomment and set tokens directly in the TOML config.

Logging
-------
Logs to /var/log/clapshot-slack-unfurl/unfurl.log (directory managed by
systemd's LogsDirectory=). Logrotate config installed to
/etc/logrotate.d/clapshot-slack-unfurl (weekly, 4 rotations, compressed).
Sends SIGHUP to reopen log file after rotation.

Security
--------
The systemd unit runs with ProtectSystem=strict, ProtectHome=true,
NoNewPrivileges=true, and PrivateTmp=true. The service only needs
read access to Clapshot's data directory and outbound network for
Slack Socket Mode.

Channel allowlist in the TOML config controls which Slack channels
receive unfurls. An empty list denies all channels.

Example config: /usr/share/doc/clapshot-slack-unfurl/clapshot-slack-unfurl.toml.example
